# DECK 00 — the TEMPLATE. A real, working three-slide deck whose subject is its own skeleton:
# copy this directory, rename it `NN-topic`, add the `- *: NN-topic` pointer to
# ../.yamlover/body.yamlover, and rewrite the slides. The rules it describes are the series
# rules; the file itself is the example of them. Spec: ../../CHAPTER.md.
!!<*yamlover: $defs: chapter>
The deck template
description: Copy this folder, rename it, rewrite the slides — the rules are in the slides
- What a deck is
  notes: |
    This slide is here so the template can be watched as a deck, not only read as a file.

    Say: a deck is one directory holding one file. The directory exists so a screenshot
    can be dropped in later without moving anything; the file is a yamlover chapter whose
    subchapters are the slides.
  - |
    One directory, one file — `.yamlover/body.yamlover`, a chapter tagged
    `!!<*yamlover: $defs: chapter>` whose **subchapters are the slides**.
  - |
    Seven slides, four to six minutes, one idea. The deck root carries a **title** and a
    **`description`** and nothing else — so the tree on the left reads as the slide list.
- What a slide is
  notes: |
    Read the code block out loud if this is ever recorded; otherwise this slide is
    reference material for the author.

    Say: a slide is a subchapter. Its own value is the title. `description` is the
    optional one-line takeaway under it. `notes:` is what you say — the chapter renderer
    draws the title, the description and the body, and ignores every other keyed entry,
    so the script is in the file and never on the screen. Then one to three body chunks,
    forty words at the very most, because the screen belongs to the app.
  - !!<format: text/markdown> |
    ```yamlover
    - A slide title                    # the subchapter's self-value
      description: the one takeaway    # optional, renders as a subtitle
      notes: |                         # THE SPOKEN SCRIPT — never rendered
        Open examples/… and click …
      - |
        At most forty words of **marklower** on screen.
    ```
- Rules worth not breaking
  notes: |
    Say: four of them, and they are all consequences of how the renderer works rather
    than taste.
  - !!<*yamlover: $defs: bullets>
    - '`notes:` goes on slides only — a keyed entry at the root of a directory overlay is a member overlay, and would show up as a phantom `notes` child'
    - demo paths belong in `notes:`, not in the slide body, so a deck stays readable on its own
    - no `:[i]` links between slides — a keyed entry consumes an index, so inserting a slide would retarget them
    - a cell or a line that starts with `*` must be quoted, or the parser reads a pointer
  - |
    Structure comes from the taxonomy, not from prose: a comparison is a `table` node, a
    list is a `bullets` or `numbered` node, a diagram is a `text/x-plantuml` chunk.
